00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.435
- I asked on Twitter,
a little Twitter poll,

00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:05.205
have any of you actually
lied to the pollsters,

00:00:05.205 --> 00:00:06.906
about your support for Trump?

00:00:06.906 --> 00:00:09.476
Hundreds of people said yes.

00:00:09.476 --> 00:00:11.711 align:start size:84% position:16%
And they weren't
saying we might lie,

00:00:11.711 --> 00:00:14.314 align:start size:84% position:16%
or we think we'll
do it in the future,

00:00:14.314 --> 00:00:17.283
they said we have, this year.

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:19.886
(upbeat music)

00:00:28.762 --> 00:00:30.697 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
- It's Locals week, here
on the Rubin Report,

00:00:30.697 --> 00:00:32.632 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
and I'm doing a series
of mini interviews

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:34.968 line:0%
with creators, on why
they decided to become

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:36.569
less reliant on big tech,

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:39.039
and instead own their
content, community,

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:41.641
and livelihood with Locals.com.

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:43.943
Joining me today, is the
creator of the legendary

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:45.345
"Dilbert" comic strip,

00:00:45.345 --> 00:00:47.480
as well as a best selling author

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:50.316
and guy who really,
really loves coffee,

00:00:50.316 --> 00:00:51.584
Scott Adams.

00:00:51.584 --> 00:00:53.186
Welcome back to
the Rubin Report.

00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:54.020
- Thanks, Dave.

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:55.288
Thanks for having me.

00:00:55.288 --> 00:00:56.289
- How much coffee
do you drink a day?

00:00:56.289 --> 00:00:57.490
I always think you're just

00:00:57.490 --> 00:01:00.393 align:start size:84% position:16%
drinking coffee
constantly, basically.

00:01:00.393 --> 00:01:02.262
- Christina, my wife
gave me a new trick,

00:01:02.262 --> 00:01:04.097
where I only do half coffee,

00:01:04.097 --> 00:01:05.999
and half hot water,

00:01:05.999 --> 00:01:09.969 align:start position:0%
and instead of coffee, it's
like a coffee flavored beverage

00:01:09.969 --> 00:01:11.438
that you can drink more of it.

00:01:11.438 --> 00:01:14.307 align:start size:97% position:3%
So, that's my curtain trick
for doubling my output.

00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:16.876 align:start size:97% position:3%
- I think that's a little
bit like an Americano, right?

00:01:16.876 --> 00:01:18.344
Isn't that when you go to Europe

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:19.813
and you drink an Americano?

00:01:19.813 --> 00:01:21.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's just coffee and they
just add water to it,

00:01:21.581 --> 00:01:22.649
I think, maybe.

00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:25.118
- I don't know my coffees,

00:01:25.118 --> 00:01:26.953
but I'm gonna say yes.

00:01:26.953 --> 00:01:28.555
I'm just gonna say yes to that.

00:01:28.555 --> 00:01:30.924
- You got very Long Island
there when you said coffee.

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:33.660 align:start size:84% position:16%
Your coffee, you don't
know your coffee.

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:34.928
- Well, I'm Upstate New York,

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:38.031
so we drink coffee and
we go off on the roof,

00:01:38.031 --> 00:01:40.467
and down by the creek.

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:41.901
- All right.

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:43.436
- We go swimming in the creek.

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:44.737
- Well, I'm gonna send you one
of these Locals coffee mugs,

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:45.805
we've got one.

00:01:45.805 --> 00:01:47.307
But before we get into Locals,

00:01:47.307 --> 00:01:50.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you've absolutely
just crushed it on there,

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:53.480 align:start position:0%
um, I wanted to talk about
something separate all together.

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:56.483
Which is that because we
live in this strange time,

00:01:56.483 --> 00:01:59.085
where it seems no one can
make sense of anything,

00:01:59.085 --> 00:02:01.654 align:start size:88% position:13%
you're one of the people
on a very short list,

00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:04.157
that can probably
do it on one hand.

00:02:04.157 --> 00:02:08.294 align:start size:97% position:3%
People who I think are
actually making some sense.

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:10.663 align:start size:97% position:3%
Did you ever think you were
gonna be a sense-maker?

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:12.465
I mean, that's partly what

00:02:12.465 --> 00:02:14.734
being a comic guy is.

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:16.069
You're making little quips,

00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:17.537 align:start size:88% position:13%
and you're trying to
make sense of the world.

00:02:17.537 --> 00:02:20.340
But did you ever think it was
gonna be this level of it?

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:23.176 align:start size:97% position:3%
- You're asking me the
most embarrassing questions

00:02:23.176 --> 00:02:24.110
you possibly could,

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:25.645
because the answer is yes.

00:02:25.645 --> 00:02:28.414
- Ah, you're supposed
to be humble here.

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:29.582
- Yeah, I know.

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:31.117 line:0%
The answer's yes

00:02:31.117 --> 00:02:33.319 line:0%
and my whole life, actually.

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:36.022 line:0%
So, I always had an image

00:02:36.022 --> 00:02:37.290
that some day,

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:39.325
I didn't know what
path I would take,

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:41.861 align:start size:94% position:6%
but that I would be doing
something in public,

00:02:41.861 --> 00:02:44.297 align:start size:97% position:3%
in which I would be
explaining things to people

00:02:44.297 --> 00:02:47.367
who needed a little help
having things explained.

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:52.338 align:start size:97% position:3%
So, it's amazing that it
ended up the way it ended up.

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:54.841 align:start size:97% position:3%
Cause the way I got here
could not have been predicted

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:55.875
in any way.

00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:57.744
But yes, the answer is

00:02:57.744 --> 00:03:00.013
I did see my future
exactly like this.

00:03:00.013 --> 00:03:01.314
- Yeah, are you shocked though,

00:03:01.314 --> 00:03:04.384
to see that the general
systems of sense-making,

00:03:04.384 --> 00:03:07.287
our institutions, the media,
the rest of the stuff that

00:03:07.287 --> 00:03:10.390
guys like us spend most
of our day talking about?

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:13.693
Are you shocked to see how
rapidly they've crumbled,

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:14.928
or is this,

00:03:14.928 --> 00:03:16.462
is this just the
last gasp of air?

00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:18.364 align:start size:84% position:16%
Like, what's
happening right now?

00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:20.099
- Well, I think Trump uh,

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:23.603 align:start size:97% position:3%
took the last bit of
credibility outta the system.

00:03:23.603 --> 00:03:26.806 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, all he did was reveal
what the system was.

00:03:26.806 --> 00:03:28.675 align:start size:81% position:19%
I don't think that
he changed it,

00:03:28.675 --> 00:03:31.010
as much as he revealed it,

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:32.445
and then we could see it.

00:03:32.445 --> 00:03:35.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, who knows how corrupt
the news used to be.

00:03:35.682 --> 00:03:38.384
I used to hear stories
back in Kennedy's day

00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:40.687
of the Kennedy would
go out in the yacht

00:03:40.687 --> 00:03:41.955
and the take uh,

00:03:41.955 --> 00:03:43.156
take the New York Times,

00:03:43.156 --> 00:03:45.024
or the other top
reporters with him.

00:03:45.024 --> 00:03:46.859
And did he get good coverage?

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:47.827
Of course he did.

00:03:47.827 --> 00:03:48.661
(chuckling)

00:03:48.661 --> 00:03:49.762
Of course he did.

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:51.831
So, things are different,

00:03:51.831 --> 00:03:54.067 align:start size:84% position:16%
but I dunno if
they're more corrupt.

00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:56.536
I think we just might be
a little more aware of it.

00:03:56.536 --> 00:03:58.304
And the thing that Trump did,

00:03:58.304 --> 00:04:00.373
is he just completely just said,

00:04:00.373 --> 00:04:02.542
I think I'll just say
whatever I wanna say,

00:04:02.542 --> 00:04:05.478 align:start size:84% position:16%
as long as it leads
me in a productive way

00:04:05.478 --> 00:04:06.980
that's good for the country.

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:08.881
Didn't worry about the facts,

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:10.316
and it didn't hurt him at all.

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:12.118
He became president doing that,

00:04:12.118 --> 00:04:13.253
when everybody was saying,

00:04:13.253 --> 00:04:14.721
well, you can't be president,

00:04:14.721 --> 00:04:16.823
if you keep saying things
that the fact-checkers

00:04:16.823 --> 00:04:17.657
don't agree with.

00:04:17.657 --> 00:04:18.925
And then he did.

00:04:18.925 --> 00:04:20.760 align:start size:88% position:13%
And he proved that it
didn't matter that much.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:22.595
- So, didn't worry
about the facts.

00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:24.564
When people criticize you,

00:04:24.564 --> 00:04:26.065
or they criticize me,

00:04:26.065 --> 00:04:28.101
or some of the other people
that are just walking around.

00:04:28.101 --> 00:04:30.470 align:start size:97% position:3%
Not even that are necessarily
rah-rah Trump people,

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:33.106
but just don't suffer from
Trump derangement syndrome.

00:04:33.106 --> 00:04:34.374
That's the thing,

00:04:34.374 --> 00:04:35.875
the facts, the facts,
the facts, the facts.

00:04:35.875 --> 00:04:38.144
How do you, I've heard you
explain it a little bit,

00:04:38.144 --> 00:04:39.846
but how do you explain his,

00:04:39.846 --> 00:04:43.283 align:start size:94% position:6%
sort of loose relationship
with the facts?

00:04:43.283 --> 00:04:46.386
- Well, I call it uh,
directionally accurate.

00:04:46.386 --> 00:04:48.421
So, if Trump says
something like,

00:04:48.421 --> 00:04:51.324 align:start size:88% position:13%
well, there were 40,000
people at my rally,

00:04:51.324 --> 00:04:53.493
but the real number was 25,000,

00:04:53.493 --> 00:04:55.695
that's kinda the same, right?

00:04:55.695 --> 00:04:57.597
It doesn't change how
you think about it.

00:04:57.597 --> 00:04:59.332 align:start size:81% position:19%
A lot of people
came to the rally.

00:04:59.332 --> 00:05:00.133
How much should it have been?

00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:01.634
Well, I dunno.

00:05:01.634 --> 00:05:05.805
If he says the economy is the
best economy we've ever had,

00:05:05.805 --> 00:05:09.876
but it's only the best
one in the last 40 years,

00:05:09.876 --> 00:05:12.679
does that help us or
does that hurt us?

00:05:12.679 --> 00:05:13.913
Well, it helps us,

00:05:13.913 --> 00:05:16.883
because the economy is
a psychology engine,

00:05:16.883 --> 00:05:18.084
as I like to say.

00:05:18.084 --> 00:05:19.552
If you think it's doing well,

00:05:19.552 --> 00:05:21.888
you invest, you buy,
you have confidence.

00:05:21.888 --> 00:05:23.323
And then it does well.

00:05:23.323 --> 00:05:26.259 align:start size:84% position:16%
So, he has the ability
to use hyperbole,

00:05:26.259 --> 00:05:28.294
and a little bit
of exaggeration,

00:05:28.294 --> 00:05:30.029
to make things work

00:05:30.029 --> 00:05:32.098 align:start size:94% position:6%
better than they would've
worked without it.

00:05:32.098 --> 00:05:34.801 align:start size:97% position:3%
Which is completely different
than a flat out lie,

00:05:34.801 --> 00:05:37.203
like let's say that
the fine people hoax,

00:05:37.203 --> 00:05:39.539 align:start size:81% position:19%
that's nothing but
a divisive lie.

00:05:39.539 --> 00:05:41.240
That's a bad,

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:43.543
missing the fact checking.

00:05:43.543 --> 00:05:45.144
That's as bad as you can get.

00:05:45.144 --> 00:05:47.413
But, if you're just
talking something up

00:05:47.413 --> 00:05:49.148 align:start size:88% position:13%
that needs to be
talked up, that's fine.

00:05:49.148 --> 00:05:50.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Yeah, I actually wasn't
gonna bring this up,

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:52.085
but let's just do it real quick,

00:05:52.085 --> 00:05:53.219
before we get to your community.

00:05:53.219 --> 00:05:54.587
The very fine people hoax.

00:05:54.587 --> 00:05:55.988
You were one of
the first people,

00:05:55.988 --> 00:05:59.692
at least, sort of like
mainstream-ish people,

00:05:59.692 --> 00:06:01.928 align:start size:84% position:16%
or someone with come
cred, let's say,

00:06:01.928 --> 00:06:04.230
that was calling out the
very fine people hoax,

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:08.167
and pointing out
that before he said

00:06:08.167 --> 00:06:09.569
very fine people on both sides,

00:06:09.569 --> 00:06:12.438
which he meant about
the monument argument

00:06:12.438 --> 00:06:14.040
in and of itself, that really,

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:16.442
he had condemned the white
nationalists and the KKK

00:06:16.442 --> 00:06:18.311
the sentence before.

00:06:18.311 --> 00:06:20.146
Biden has said that
this is the reason

00:06:20.146 --> 00:06:21.914 align:start size:81% position:19%
that he is running
for president,

00:06:21.914 --> 00:06:23.716
yet the media doesn't
call him out on it.

00:06:23.716 --> 00:06:24.917
- I dunno.

00:06:24.917 --> 00:06:26.486
- Does anything shock
you at this point?

00:06:26.486 --> 00:06:28.755
- I really don't understand

00:06:28.755 --> 00:06:31.224 align:start size:84% position:16%
if the media doesn't
know it's a lie,

00:06:31.224 --> 00:06:34.193 align:start size:97% position:3%
because they've been reporting
it as true for so long,

00:06:34.193 --> 00:06:36.095 align:start size:84% position:16%
and they all believe
that they saw it.

00:06:36.095 --> 00:06:37.296
They saw it with their own eyes,

00:06:37.296 --> 00:06:38.765
heard it with their own ears.

00:06:38.765 --> 00:06:40.733 align:start size:94% position:6%
And what they saw and
heard was the edited part.

00:06:40.733 --> 00:06:42.235
- [Dave] Right.

00:06:42.235 --> 00:06:44.203
- Where they take out the
sentence where he clarified

00:06:44.203 --> 00:06:46.439 align:start size:97% position:3%
that he totally wasn't
talking about those people.

00:06:46.439 --> 00:06:47.640
- [Dave] Yeah.

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:48.574
- In the clear, clear
as possible words.

00:06:48.574 --> 00:06:49.876
They just leave that out.

00:06:49.876 --> 00:06:51.377
And that is misleading.

00:06:51.377 --> 00:06:54.180
So uh, the fact that
the media does that

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:55.615
is still puzzling to me,

00:06:55.615 --> 00:06:58.317 align:start size:84% position:16%
'cause I can't tell
how intentional it is,

00:06:58.317 --> 00:07:00.987 align:start position:0%
or if they're really just
fooled by their own propaganda.

00:07:00.987 --> 00:07:01.821
- Right.

00:07:01.821 --> 00:07:02.989
- It's hard to tell.

00:07:02.989 --> 00:07:04.490 align:start size:84% position:16%
- It's kinda, I
always think it's like

00:07:04.490 --> 00:07:05.858
they've gone so deep with it
and repeated it so many times,

00:07:05.858 --> 00:07:07.527
that it would be just too,

00:07:07.527 --> 00:07:09.162 align:start size:84% position:16%
it would like
shatter their world,

00:07:09.162 --> 00:07:11.364
basically, if they had to
admit that it wasn't true,

00:07:11.364 --> 00:07:12.865
with something like that.

00:07:12.865 --> 00:07:14.767
- Yeah, that's why uh,

00:07:14.767 --> 00:07:16.636 align:start size:84% position:16%
Trump basically could
win the election

00:07:16.636 --> 00:07:20.173 align:start size:84% position:16%
