00:13:09.221 --> 00:13:11.924 align:start position:0%
we've taken all of these
things to their end conclusion.

00:13:11.924 --> 00:13:15.394 align:start size:84% position:16%
And that the internet
of 2024, 2025

00:13:15.394 --> 00:13:17.563
is gonna be way, way different

00:13:17.563 --> 00:13:19.398 align:start size:84% position:16%
than what we're
looking at right now.

00:13:20.766 --> 00:13:24.270
- Well, I've argued that
artificial intelligence

00:13:24.270 --> 00:13:26.906
has already taken
over the world.

00:13:26.906 --> 00:13:30.109
Um, it's just not exactly the
way we thought it would be.

00:13:30.109 --> 00:13:31.610
It's not in a robot body,

00:13:31.610 --> 00:13:33.145
it doesn't talk to us.

00:13:33.145 --> 00:13:37.249
But the algorithms of the
social media platforms,

00:13:37.249 --> 00:13:39.185
they decide what you see.

00:13:39.185 --> 00:13:41.287 align:start size:84% position:16%
And they decide based
on a simple rule,

00:13:41.287 --> 00:13:42.955 align:start size:84% position:16%
of what's gonna
make the most money,

00:13:42.955 --> 00:13:44.523
and nobody goes to jail.

00:13:44.523 --> 00:13:46.625
Just a few other considerations.

00:13:46.625 --> 00:13:48.394
And as long as that algorithm

00:13:48.394 --> 00:13:51.497
is going toward
that one outcome,

00:13:51.497 --> 00:13:54.900
it's gonna cause people to
be at each other's necks.

00:13:54.900 --> 00:13:55.868
So a lot of the,

00:13:55.868 --> 00:13:58.003
the fighting and the conflict,

00:13:58.003 --> 00:14:00.706 align:start size:84% position:16%
and the divisiveness,
comes from math,

00:14:00.706 --> 00:14:02.741
it comes from the algorithms.

00:14:02.741 --> 00:14:05.444 align:start size:88% position:13%
It's not people deciding
that we should fight,

00:14:05.444 --> 00:14:06.912
